# rush_hour — "Rush Hour" (Quest 8)
#
# GRANTED BY: the Mad Fisherman's closing choice in quests/ah_barnacles.quest, node mf_alex — the
# same choice that completes ah_barnacles. That file already pointed at East York and already sent
# the player to Alex, so the hand-off needed no new prose.
# COMPLETED BY: Mayor Zhao's last choice below, node zhao_west — which is also where the pack of
# cigarettes is paid, because a quest REWARD is the only thing in the pipeline that can give the
# player an item. That is why this quest is the journey and the pitch, and stops there.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS ONE LEG, NOT THE WHOLE ERRAND. The owner supplied two journal lines and Zhao's opening
# conversation on 2026-08-17; the second of those lines belongs to the squatters, which are now
# Quest 9. One journal line is still owed here — see the TODO on stage 1. The words are the
# owner's: do not draft them.
#
# ⚠ ALMOST NOTHING THIS QUEST NEEDS EXISTS YET. East York is not a chunk, the flats are not a
# location, Mayor Zhao has no PlacementPreset and no art, and the Red Star Workers Brigade have no
# enemy prefab. red_star_cigarettes DOES exist (Resources/Items/RedStarCigarettes.asset, a stack of
# 20) but has no icon. The full list, with what each one blocks, is in
# docs/plans/RUSH_HOUR_BUILD_LEDGER.md. This file is importable today and will produce a
# QuestDefinition, but the quest cannot be played until that ledger is worked through.
#
# ⚠ NEW KEYS: east_york_gate (the REACH marker on the road in) and mayor_zhao.

QUEST rush_hour
TITLE: Rush Hour
GIVER: The Mad Fisherman
LOCATION: East York, two chunks south through the slums.

# Stage 0 — the journey. REACH rather than TALKTO because Zhao is not sought out; he ambushes the
# player on the road in, through the proximity trigger described below. The marker key is a
# placeholder until East York exists and the arrival point is authored.
STAGE REACH east_york_gate
OBJECTIVE: Get yourself to far off lands of… east York! Apparently the Chinese have deep roots here. Maybe someone can point me in the right direction here, I'll ask around.

# Stage 1 (last) — hearing Zhao out. MANUAL, not TALKTO: a TalkTo final stage completes on the
# interact, before he says a word, which would pay the cigarettes and end the quest as he opens his
# mouth. Same reasoning as spark_of_talent and gangbusters.
STAGE MANUAL
OBJECTIVE: [TODO: one journal line for the beat between arriving in East York and the end of Zhao's pitch.]

# ⚠ THE QUEST ENDS WHERE THE CIGARETTES CHANGE HANDS, and that is not a style choice.
# A quest REWARD is the only way to give the player an item, and it pays once, on completion — a
# DialogueChoice's ITEM: is a REQUIREMENT, not a grant. investigate_weird_vape.quest hit exactly
# this wall with Daniel's Big Blue and solved it the same way: end the quest at the handover and
# make the next leg its own quest. So Rush Hour is the journey to East York and Zhao's pitch;
# the squatters are Quest 9.
#
# ⚠ UNWRITTEN, and deliberately absent rather than guessed at:
#   - the stage 1 objective above
#   - Quest 9: the squatters, and how "have a word, or several" resolves — a fight? a conversation?
#     paying them off? Its journal line already exists in the owner's text and is parked here so it
#     is not lost: "Find the North Korean squatters and show them how we protect our glorious
#     landlords."
#   - Zhao's second conversation, where he honours the bargain and points at Ralph and Sanjeet
#   - the beat that actually finds Ralph and Sanjeet, which is what the arc has been building to
# Add  GRANT: <quest 9 id>  beside the COMPLETE: below once Quest 9 exists.

# 150 XP is a placeholder chosen to sit above ah_barnacles' 120. No pounds: Zhao pays in a pack of
# cigarettes and a favour owed.
REWARD
XP: 150
# The pack of 20. This is what makes Zhao's "Take this for help!" true — it lands as the
# conversation closes and the completion notice appears, which is the only moment the pipeline can
# give an item at all.
ITEM: red_star_cigarettes x20

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mayor Zhao.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS PROXIMITY DIALOGUE, AND NOTHING IN THE PROJECT FIRES IT YET. Every conversation today
# is opened by the player pressing USE on an Interactable. Zhao's is meant to start on its own as
# the player walks into East York, which needs a new ProximityDialogueTrigger component on a
# trigger collider across the road in. See the ledger.
#
# ⚠ THE RE-FIRE PROBLEM IS THE HARD PART, NOT THE FIRING. A chunk is destroyed and rebuilt on every
# entry (ChunkManager.TravelRoutine), so a plain "already seen this" bool on the component resets
# and Zhao ambushes the player every single time they walk into East York, forever. The fix that
# needs no new save field is to gate the trigger on quest state: fire only while rush_hour is
# active AND sitting on stage 0. Reaching the marker advances the stage, which disarms the trigger
# by itself and keeps it disarmed across saves.
#
# THE CIGARETTES ARE THE QUEST REWARD, paid as this conversation closes. See the REWARD block
# above for why that is the only place they can come from.

DIALOGUE mayorzhao

NODE start
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: KONICHIWA BROTHERMAN!
CHOICE Konichiwa? -> zhao_china

NODE zhao_china
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: Yes my fine feathered friend! This is as close to China as you can be without jetting off to Beijing herself!
CHOICE Understood, but konichiwa is Japanese. -> zhao_correction

NODE zhao_correction
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: OOOOOH OKAY. Who do you think knows real Chinese? Mayor Zhao or … ? Yeah. So konichiwa foreigner!
CHOICE … -> zhao_honour

NODE zhao_honour
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: We don't get too many folks coming to see us so it's an honour!
CHOICE Well I'm just looking for.. -> zhao_favour

NODE zhao_favour
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: WELL BEFORE YOU ASK ME FOR SOMETHING.. Allow Zhao to ask you for a favour.
CHOICE [Sighs] -> zhao_brigade

NODE zhao_brigade
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: I require a little issue resolving. I hired a plucky little Asian start up to begin the build on a few blocks of flats just outside the city, for the comrades in need.
CHOICE [Continue listening] -> zhao_kim

NODE zhao_kim
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: Well apparently Red Star Workers Brigade have ties to Mr Kim. They've been building the flats no issue, lovely.
CHOICE [Continue listening] -> zhao_squatters

NODE zhao_squatters
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: BUT NOW THEY WONT LEAVE. They're living in them! Please. Have a word, or several. Anything! Then we can talk about your request, you will go to the prom Cinderella.
CHOICE What? -> zhao_west

NODE zhao_west
SPEAKER: mayorzhao
SPEAK: GO! It's west from here. Take this for help!
# No -> : this ends the conversation, completes the quest, and pays the reward — the 150 XP and the
# pack of Red Star cigarettes Zhao just offered.
CHOICE Okay.
COMPLETE: rush_hour
